/-!
# Levi-fixed lifts for the quadratic-splitting argument

The conjugate-axis construction supplies P-fixed lifts of every vector on the
literal quotient line. The displacement-cocycle calculation and odd-index
averaging then construct K-fixed lifts from two explicit matrix-geometry
inputs. The fixed-line-vector and local-complement applications retain the
original submodule and quotient map.

Unconditional B.4.9(1) Levi lifting still requires the actual binary Levi
coordinates and the rank-one seed index. The source assembly remains here;
none of the re-exported conditional results assumes fixed lifting or splitting.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
B.4.9(1), printed pp.92–93.
-/
